  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Vitamin A Deficiency: Xerophthalmia: With this condition, the eyes may become very dry and crusted, which may damage the cornea and retina.</p><p>Thiamine Deficiency: Beriberi is a disease in which the body does not have enough thiamine (vitamin B1).</p><p>Scurvy is a disease caused by a serious vitamin C(Ascorbic acid) deficiency</p><p>Riboflavin deficiency is often associated with cheilosis (chapping and fissuring of the lips). Riboflavin Deficiency. Riboflavin deficiency can be associated with various developmental abnormalities, including cleft lip.</p></blockquote>",
